#
# Line endings are part of the package identity, so they are pinned here.
#
# Conan hashes the exported sources to get the recipe revision. Without this
# file the working tree gets whatever the platform's git defaults produce, and a
# checkout that converts text to CRLF exports different bytes — so the same
# commit yields a different recipe revision, and one release publishes several.
# That is not hypothetical: `release/0.8.1` published 9fbdb476… from Linux and
# macOS and cd1d5b96… from Windows.
#
# eol=lf normalises the working tree on every platform, not only the index, and
# the working tree is what gets exported.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and must never be touched. `text=auto` detects these correctly on its
# own; naming them is a guard against a future rule that is less careful.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary

# The compatibility fixtures. `text=auto` does detect these correctly today —
# they are full of NUL bytes — but the detection is a heuristic over the first
# few kilobytes, and these files exist precisely to be byte-for-byte what an
# earlier build wrote. A normalisation applied to one of them would not corrupt
# it visibly; it would change a digest the suite then reports as a format change.
tests/fixtures/** binary

# Except the manifest, which is the one file here meant to be read. It is the
# certificate a reviewer compares against when fixtures are regenerated, and a
# diff they cannot see is a diff they cannot check. Kept out of the rule above
# rather than left to detection, and with its line endings pinned so that what it
# certifies does not depend on which platform committed it.
tests/fixtures/**/manifest.json -binary text eol=lf
